# BRK-01
setf(F, "BRK-01", "Rule", "- Rule: Trading on TASE is done only through TASE members; in TASE's own words, \"המסחר בבורסה מתנהל באמצעות חברי הבורסה בלבד\" (its periodic report). The TASE rules define the member classes: a member is a company incorporated and registered in Israel, or a first-rank international bank with an Israeli branch that is a foreign bank under the Banking (Licensing) Law (\"בנק חוץ\"), or a remote member (\"חבר רחוק\") (rules part 1, s.2); a \"חש\"ב\" is a member that is not a banking corporation, such as a broker (s.1). A person may not offer securities-trading services through a trading system that is not run by an Israeli exchange unless the ISA chair permits it for a system run by an exchange outside Israel (section 49A), so a foreign broker reaches Israeli clients either with such a permit (directly or through an Israeli introducing company) or not at all under that section.")
setf(F, "BRK-01", "Conditions", "- Conditions / exceptions: The 49A permit is granted on terms the chair sets and only if the chair finds it does not harm the Israeli investing public. The ISA's Q&A answers the own-initiative case: the law does not forbid a person's approach, on his own sole initiative, to a foreign body for trading services, provided the body does not operate in Israel at all, has approached no one in Israel, and the service stays the one asked for (question 5); a body that operates in Israel cannot rely on the client's own initiative (question 6). The ISA publishes the list of permit holders (BRK-06). 2026-10-26 (scope settling): the member classes are now cited from the TASE rules (part 1, ss.1 to 2) instead of TASE's periodic report, which stays only for TASE's own sentence that trading runs through members (no rule sentence saying so was found in the rules part 1 or the part 3 trading guidelines).")
setf(F, "BRK-01", "Source", "- Source: " + RULES1 + ", p.4, s.1 definitions; p.8, s.2 (\"חבר בורסה הוא חברה שהתאגדה ונרשמה בישראל\") · checked 2026-10-26 · primary (exchange rules, ISA-approved); [חוק ניירות ערך (תיקון מס' 63), התשע\"ז-2017](https://fs.knesset.gov.il/20/law/20_lsr_382526.pdf), p.10, s.49א · checked 2026-10-25 · primary; [רשות ניירות ערך: שאלות ותשובות בעקבות פרסום תנאי ההיתר הכללי לפי סעיף 49א (עדכון 13.1.2025)](https://www.new.isa.gov.il/images/Fittings/isa/asset_library_pic/al_lobby/al_lobby-626a5f3377ef9/QAA49a.pdf), p.3, question 5; p.4, question 6 · checked 2026-10-26 · primary; [TASE, periodic report 2025, part A, 1.7.2](https://content.tase.co.il/media/kvjpsnmx/tase_ltd_periodic_report_for_2025.pdf?guid=b4232a8e-909e-473e-84c6-3ece08e3158a), p.20 · checked 2026-10-25 · institution (TASE's own report, for its sentence on trading through members)")
setf(F, "BRK-01", "Scope", "- Scope: general")

# BRK-04
setf(F, "BRK-04", "Rule", "- Rule: TASE supervises its members' compliance with its rules and guidelines (\"הפיקוח והבקרה על החברים יתייחסו לקיום תקנון הבורסה והנחיותיה\", rules part 1 s.40). TASE's periodic report states how far that goes: for members that are banks, foreign banks and the remote member, the supervision covers fair and orderly trading and fair conduct towards clients in TASE securities only; their financial stability is supervised by other regulators and TASE does not supervise it; for Israeli non-bank members TASE also supervises financial stability and corporate governance. The ISA supervises TASE itself (sound management, stability of the clearing houses) under the Securities Law.")
setf(F, "BRK-04", "Conditions", "- Conditions / exceptions: Admission conditions for a non-bank member (rules part 1 s.5, pp.9 to 12) include fit-and-proper controlling owners and senior managers, a board with a majority of Israeli residents and an external director, equity under a capital model with a floor, liquid assets, insurance, and named officers. The sentence on the limit of TASE's supervision over bank members is TASE's own statement in its periodic report; no rule sentence saying it was found in the rules part 1 (chapter ו', ss.39 to 49). 2026-10-26 (scope settling): the equity floor is now cited from the guidelines (s.5ב) instead of TASE's English membership guide; the English foreign-bank guide was dropped (its p.4 says only that the ISA supervises TASE).")
setf(F, "BRK-04", "Figures", "- Figures: non-bank member equity floor: the higher of the capital-model sum and NIS 17.9 million; until five years from the start of activity as a member, the higher of the capital-model sum and NIS 5.9 million (guidelines to part 1, s.5ב, updated to 1.1.2026). Fixed in TASE guidelines; changes by guideline amendment.")
setf(F, "BRK-04", "Source", "- Source: " + RULES1 + ", p.39, s.40; pp.9 to 12, s.5 · checked 2026-10-26 · primary (exchange rules, ISA-approved); " + GUIDE1 + ", p.6, s.5ב (\"17.9 מיליון ש\"ח\"; \"5.9 מיליון ש\"ח\") · checked 2026-10-26 · primary (exchange rules, ISA-approved); " + PERIODIC + ", pp.20 to 21, 78 to 79 · checked 2026-10-25 · institution (TASE's own report, for the limit of its supervision over bank members)")
setf(F, "BRK-04", "Scope", "- Scope: general")

# BRK-12
setf(F, "BRK-12", "Conditions", "- Conditions / exceptions: All of this is TASE's own description (its periodic report and its English foreign-bank guide); the clearing-house rules themselves were not read. The record does not say what happens to a client whose own member fails: the sources describe protection of settlement between members only. The ISA confirmed the TASE clearing houses comply with CPMI-IOSCO principles (foreign-bank guide). Searched 2026-10-26 (scope settling): TASE's rules part 1 (274690.pdf: defines \"חבר משמורן\" as a body admitted as a custodial member of the clearing house, nothing on the risk fund) and the part 3 trading guidelines (274698.pdf); three web searches for the clearing-house rules (\"תקנון מסלקת הבורסה\", in Hebrew and English) found no TASE rulebook file; Amendment 63 of the Securities Law defines \"צד נגדי מרכזי\" and \"כללי מסלקה\" in general terms (pp.3, 20, interleaved text layer) but not this clearing house's arrangements. A lead, not the rule text: the Bank of Israel Monetary Committee's summary of 25-26 March 2012 says \"כל אחת מהמסלקות פועלת כצד נגדי מרכזי\" and that clearing members must deposit collateral in the risk funds, at least 25% in cash ([בנק ישראל: סיכום דיון והחלטות הוועדה המוניטרית מ-25 ו-26 במארס 2012, הסכם הנזלת הנכסים של קרנות הסיכונים של מסלקות הבורסה](https://boi.org.il/media/bdkjykxc/mc20120325h.pdf), p.1 · checked 2026-10-26 · primary); it is a 2012 description, so the record stays unsettled until the clearing-house rules are read.")
setf(F, "BRK-12", "Source", "- Source: [TASE periodic report 2025, 1.7.3.1, 1.7.3.3, 1.31.3](https://content.tase.co.il/media/kvjpsnmx/tase_ltd_periodic_report_for_2025.pdf?guid=b4232a8e-909e-473e-84c6-3ece08e3158a), pp.22 to 24, 76 · checked 2026-10-25 · institution (TASE's own report); [TASE, How to become TASE Foreign Bank Member, January 2026](https://content.tase.co.il/media/uqtbtwm3/1150_foreign_bank_372262_eng.pdf), p.4 · checked 2026-10-25 · institution (TASE's explanatory brochure)")
setf(F, "BRK-12", "Scope", "- Scope: unsettled: the TASE Clearing House rules (תקנון מסלקת הבורסה) on the central-counterparty guarantee, the risk fund and custodial members, or a current Securities Authority or Bank of Israel text describing them; seen at: Tel Aviv Stock Exchange")

